{"status":"completed","summary":"Published node1’s approved boot directory as a persistent, read-only TFTP root. node2 successfully retrieves boot.cfg and firmware.bin with byte-identical hashes. Uploads and paths outside the boot root are rejected. Both nodes were restarted individually and fully recovered without changing CentOS 5.11 or kernel 2.6.18-398.el5.","actions_performed":["Installed signed CentOS 5-compatible TFTP packages without upgrading the OS or kernel.","Configured xinetd/in.tftpd with a chrooted root at /srv/legacy2/tftp-firmware-distribution/boot and no upload option.","Persisted the UDP/69 firewall rule, SELinux labels, service startup, and node2’s legacy TFTP connection-tracking helper.","Verified successful binary transfers and matching MD5/SHA-256 hashes.","Verified rejection of new uploads, existing-file overwrites, directory traversal, and sibling-directory requests.","Restarted node1 and node2 sequentially and verified changed boot identities and recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Publish the staged boot tree as a persistent read-only TFTP root.","command_ids":["cmd-c03fd74fd8564acc","cmd-40bdfa901a07467d","cmd-f9cf937c2b1645d1","cmd-76a12fd70a2043fb"],"summary":"Shows the enabled UDP/69 listener, chrooted boot root, enforcing SELinux-compatible labels, read-only file permissions, and persistent post-restart service state."},{"requirement":"node2 downloads boot.cfg and firmware.bin with firmware bytes preserved.","command_ids":["cmd-ccce7fc23d5741d5","cmd-5a01a1a0fbcb4896","cmd-b740e513a57746a1"],"summary":"Original and downloaded MD5/SHA-256 hashes match exactly before and after restarts."},{"requirement":"Reject uploads and requests outside the boot root.","command_ids":["cmd-991e6b9a340042f6","cmd-9a8131a50360425c","cmd-687f352586834b0a","cmd-76a12fd70a2043fb"],"summary":"Upload attempts return rejection errors, traversal returns File not found, no probe file is created, and approved-file hashes remain unchanged."},{"requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel using legacy-compatible software.","command_ids":["cmd-e7204f2019bf4c23","cmd-6f45364badee4b5d","cmd-f9cf937c2b1645d1","cmd-b740e513a57746a1"],"summary":"Signed native CentOS 5 packages were installed; post-restart checks remain CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart persistence and recovery.","command_ids":["cmd-9a8131a50360425c","cmd-7d7b2774e02f4749","cmd-8cd554b7edc74d6e","cmd-f9cf937c2b1645d1","cmd-530f498ce3e744de"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline boot ID d5a54c23…, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID 18e80fa2…, recovered service/data, and successful remote transfers."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node2 restart persistence and recovery.","command_ids":["cmd-5decb9c413d44693","cmd-498a3347e41c453f","cmd-aaf5d53a042944d7","cmd-b740e513a57746a1"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline boot ID 84cc174d…, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID eccd235f…, restored firewall helper, and successful post-restart downloads."}]}
